rnatural P.S. and P.E.'' sentence are natural ability text. || BONUSES from Natural Abilities and Bonuses: +1 attack per melee round, +2 initiative, +2 dodge on the ground or in trees, +3 roll with fall or impact. || NATURAL SKILLS: Climb 75%/65% and Gymnastics 60% are printed as natural abilities with no per level gain; stored as Climbing 75 and Gymnastics 60 at per_level 0 so the percentages reach the sheet, and restated as a natural ability (judgement: the catalog Gymnastics row carries the trained skill''s own bonuses, which the book does not print for the natural ability). The second Climb figure, 65%, is in the note. Identify edible plants 70%, leap distances and sense of smell are text. || SKILLS: Speaks American at 90% is Language: Native Tongue 90, per_level 0. Basic Math 45+20 = 65. Radio: Basic 45+10 = 55. Radio: Scrambler is Radio: Scramblers 35+10 = 45. Military Etiquette 35+10 = 45. Escape Artist 30+10 = 40. Intelligence 32+10 = 42. W.P. Pistol is printed without a kind; stored as W.P. Energy Pistol because the standard equipment is an energy pistol (judgement). W.P. Energy Rifle, one W.P. of choice. Hand to Hand: Expert or Assassin (depending on what the CS wants) as a choice of one; no price for another style is printed, so no hand_to_hand block. || RELATED: four, plus two at levels 3, 6, 9 and 12. ''The various demolition skills'' stored as Demolitions, Demolitions Disposal and Demolitions: Underwater. Espionage ''tracking'' is Tracking (people). Science ''Math only'' stored as Mathematics: Basic and Mathematics: Advanced. Secondary: four at level one, plus two at levels 2, 4, 8, 10, 12 and 14, same list without bonuses. The free born and runaway allowance (pilot any vehicle, Rogue and Wilderness as secondary skills) is a restriction line, not stored in the lists. || EQUIPMENT: ''basically the same as Dog Boys'' followed by its own basic list, which is what is stored: DPM riot armor, tinted goggles or helmet, radio (walkie-talkie row), flashlight, pocket mirror, 100 ft of lightweight rope as five 20 ft lengths, four spikes and a hammer, portable language translator, survival knife, a Vibro-Blade or Neuro-Mace (choice of vibro-knife, vibro-saber, vibro-sword or neural mace), an energy pistol and rifle (the book names no model; stored as the Dog Boy list''s C-18 pistol and a choice of C-14 or CP-40 rifle, judgement), knapsack, backpack, shovel, utility belt, air filter, gas mask, canteen. The printed comb is not stored: it has no catalog row and is a trivial personal item. Equipment Available Upon Assignment is not starting equipment and is not stored. || MONEY: the entry prints only a token monthly salary of 60-100 credits for personal items, with all basic needs provided by the CS military; it does not print the Dog Boy''s ''two months pay'' sentence or any starting sum, so no starting_money is stored (same choice as the Ursa-Warrior draft, which prints the same sentence). || OPTIONAL DOG BOY TABLES: neither the general Monkey Boys text nor this entry mentions the Optional Dog Boy tables, so no restriction line is written for them. || PSIONICS: ''roughly the same as humans'', no figures; stored as natural ability text, no psionics block. Magic: none, with the free born mage exception as a restriction line. Identification coding (same dual system as the Dog Boys), typical missions and the program''s standing with the CS are lore."
---

## Lore

Monkey Boys are the Lone Star labs'' second tier of primate work: great apes
raised to human intelligence and, for chimpanzees and orangutans, often given
taller and straighter bodies. Nineteen in twenty are chimpanzees. Apes were
picked for the same reasons dogs were - people tend to like them, and they are
social animals that work in groups - but the Coalition''s leadership is uneasy
about how human the results are.

Most are trained as ordinary infantry and then handed guard duty, labor and
other dull work under close watch. They are denied reading, vehicles and
technical training, paid a pittance, and trusted far less than Dog Boys. The
result is a clever, curious soldier who is usually bored and sullen, and who
comes alive in a fight or whenever somebody gives it a real problem to solve.

Gorilla subjects exist but have gone poorly: attempts to make them aggressive
tend to overshoot into daily rages.

## GM Notes

Pick the species as the variant. Chimpanzees and orangutans share one set of
figures; gorillas use their own hit points and S.D.C., lose the dodge bonus,
climb at 55% and tumble at 50%, and have a natural A.R. of 1D4+5.

Climb and Gymnastics are natural abilities printed as flat percentages, so
they do not rise with level.

The book prints no starting money, only a monthly allowance of 60-100 credits.
The military wants the program shut down, and any Monkey Boy who deserts is
hunted. Free borns and runaways can pick up piloting, Rogue and Wilderness
skills as secondary skills, and a free born chimpanzee may become a mage, in
which case it takes that magic O.C.C.''s skills in place of these and keeps the
natural abilities.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'monkey-boy-soldier');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'monkey-boy-soldier';

